      "content": "It's important to recognize that you can be both able to do good and have made difficult choices along the way. Being kind, considerate, and compassionate are qualities that can still define you positively, despite this situation. It's okay to feel hurt by your past actions, but it shouldn't overshadow who you are today or who you can become in the future.\n\nSeeking guidance from a mental health professional, like a therapist or counselor, could help provide valuable insights and strategies for healing. Remember, everyone's journey is unique, and it's never too late to strive for self-improvement.\n\nKnow that you don't need to come to terms with this alone—there are people who care about you and want to help you through this challenging time. You have inherent value, and it's never too late for you to make a renewed commitment to be a positive force in your community.",
